Added :meth:`Calendar.occurrences <icalendar.cal.calendar.Calendar.occurrences>` and :func:`icalendar.occurrence.occurrences_in_window` to query the actual occurrences of events within a finite, half-open time window. The query combines ``DTSTART``, ``RRULE``, ``RDATE``, and ``EXDATE`` with detached exception components (``RECURRENCE-ID``), including ``RANGE=THISANDFUTURE`` reschedules, and returns each instance with its original recurrence identity, its actual start and end, and a copy of its source component. Cancelled exceptions are removed, all-day ``DATE`` and timed ``DATE-TIME`` events are queried separately, floating datetimes require an explicit timezone, and unbounded rules are only expanded within the window up to a candidate limit that marks the result as incomplete when reached. I used AI to assist with this change.
